1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 750 Tm (Introduction) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 735 Tm (Edge devices lower their clock speed when the chip gets too hot, so latency becomes erratic.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 720 Tm (Reactive governors respond only after throttling has started and cannot plan ahead.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 705 Tm (Inference workloads are often bursty, which makes short-term temperature spikes common.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 690 Tm (A scheduler that predicts temperature can delay low-priority jobs before throttling begins.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 675 Tm (Such planning must stay cheap, because the forecaster runs on the same constrained device.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 660 Tm (We therefore restrict the forecaster to a linear model that needs no accelerator support.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 645 Tm (The goal is predictable latency for interactive requests rather than maximum throughput.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 630 Tm (We compare against first-come-first-served scheduling with the default thermal governor.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 615 Tm (Our contribution is a scheduler that uses forecasts, together with measurements on devices.) Tj T* ET
.6 g
0 g
 
endstream
endobj
14 0 obj
<<
/Length 1075
>>
stream
1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 750 Tm (Methods) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 735 Tm (The forecaster is a linear model over the last 20 temperature readings sampled at 10 Hz.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 720 Tm (Jobs are deferred when the forecast exceeds 78 degrees Celsius within the next two seconds.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 705 Tm (Deferred jobs wait in a priority queue and are resumed once the forecast falls again.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 690 Tm (Interactive requests are never deferred for longer than 300 milliseconds in this design.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 675 Tm (We evaluated three device types: a phone SoC, a single-board computer and a drone controller.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 660 Tm (Each device ran the same image classification model with a batch size of one request.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 645 Tm (Every experiment lasted two hours at an ambient temperature of 24 degrees Celsius.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 35 630 Tm (Latency was logged per request, and throttling events were read from the kernel log.) Tj T* ET
.6 g
0 g
 
endstream
endobj
